  "body": "### Summary\n\nWhen `Sleep Screen` is set to `Custom`, retain the existing e-ink sleep image while waking instead of drawing the normal boot splash before restoring the reader/Home UI.\n\nThis extends CrossPoint's existing splash-suppressed/seamless display initialization behavior to custom sleep screens.\n\n### Why\n\nOn e-ink, the sleep image remains physically visible without power. Redrawing a boot splash during every normal wake creates an unnecessary intermediate refresh. Keeping the retained frame visible provides a more seamless sleep/wake experience.\n\n### Behavior\n\nBefore:\n\n`custom sleep image → CrossPoint boot splash → book/Home`\n\nAfter:\n\n`custom sleep image → book/Home`\n\nNormal cold boots and ordinary restarts continue to use the normal CrossPoint splash.\n\n### Implementation\n\nThe change intentionally reuses the existing splashless/seamless display initialization path rather than introducing new panel-driver behavior.\n\nA stale transient Quick Resume framebuffer is removed when entering Custom sleep so it cannot replace the selected custom wallpaper during wake.\n\n### Testing\n\n* clang-format 21 passes\n* cppcheck passes with no defects\n* all 130 host unit tests pass\n* the regular X4/default firmware environment builds successfully\n* the equivalent v1.5.0 implementation has been physically tested successfully on a regular Xteink X4\n\nThe `src/main.cpp` change on this branch is identical to the hardware-tested v1.5.0 patch because that upstream file has not changed since v1.5.0. This PR branch is based on current `develop` and has been built and host-tested, but the complete development-branch firmware has not itself been flashed to hardware.\n",
